Independent mesh integration and roots:
python -m pytest tests/test_nvf_interface_resolution.py -q --tb=short
11 passed in 8.69s.
The reference integrates sampled positive density in radius units and uses
Brent roots independently of the implemented Gaussian-product primitive.
The 8e-15 root comparison and derivative criteria are unchanged. The mesh
test's CDF residual assertion now includes a half-ULP root rounding term.
At radius .0001, the closest float has residual 3.008704396734174e-14;
its neighbors give -4.241051954068098e-14 and 1.0269562977782698e-13.
The production 2e-12 CDF guard, 1e-8 cell residual guard and 1e-9 Hermitian
guard are unchanged. No optical threshold or expected-failure mark changed.
The old invalid-gap replay test now rejects overlap, since gaps are supported.

